# DURABLE REPRO — `Deque` is ADMITTED to the addressable-element path but has no
# element-type arm, so `&d[i].fd` is `gg check`-clean and MEMORY-UNSAFE.
#
# THE MECHANISM. `builtins.rs` gives `Deque` `collection_kind:
# Some(CollectionKind::Array)`, so `try_resolve_index_element_ptr`'s kind-gate
# ADMITS it (the gate accepts `Array | OrderedMap`). But
# `infer_collection_element_type` strips `Vector__`, `Dict__` and `Map__` and has
# NO `Deque__` arm, so a `Deque[S]` element's type falls back to `I64_TYPE`, the
# struct-field walk finds nothing, and control falls off the field resolver —
# AFTER `lower_expr(coll)`, `lower_expr(index)` and `index_load` have all
# emitted. The result is an `int`-typed local used as a struct pointer.
#
# 🚨 BACKEND DIVERGENCE — this row behaves DIFFERENTLY on the two backends, and
# the filing must say so (measured, and UNCHANGED by the Family-1 chokepoint —
# identical before and after it):
#
#   | backend | result                                                        |
#   |---------|---------------------------------------------------------------|
#   | C       | SIGSEGV, exit 139, no output                                  |
#   | LLVM    | NO BINARY — `llc` hard-fails:                                 |
#   |         | `'%v17' defined with type 'i32' but expected 'ptr'`           |
#
# ⚠ THIS FIXTURE HAS NO LLVM LANE, and that is a documented limitation rather
# than an oversight (Core #9). On LLVM there is no binary and no output at all,
# so an output-asserting fixture cannot run there. Same shape as the in-tree
# precedent `known_gaps/sound_amp_owning_position_return.gg`, which documents its
# own C-accepts / LLVM-`llc`-fails split.
#
# ⚠ MIND THE PROBE: `gg build --backend=llvm` EXITS 0 even when `llc` FAILS (it
# prints `llc compilation failed: exit status: 1` and still returns 0). Never
# gate an LLVM probe on the shell exit code — grep the output. Verified here.
#
# INTENDED (asserted below): `IDX` printed EXACTLY ONCE, then `11`.
#
# The `IDX`-once half is the second thing this fixture pins. `Deque` is a
# REACHABLE emit-then-`None` row: the resolver emits the collection lowering, the
# index lowering and the `index_load` BEFORE returning `None`, and the caller
# then falls through to `lower_expr` and evaluates the base a SECOND time. The
# ASSIGN-face twin (`d[idx()].fd = 7`) makes that visible today as `IDX / IDX / 0`
# where the `Vector` twin prints `IDX / 7`. Accepting that double evaluation is
# the Family-1 chokepoint's deliberate disposition — the remedy ("never emit
# before you can return `None`") edits the SHARED resolvers and would change
# assign-face and method-receiver emission on their `None` paths too, which is a
# semantic change on faces the chokepoint deliberately leaves byte-identical.
#
# NOT Family-1's to fix — a Core #8 defect in its own right. Cited from TODO.md.
# Un-ignore when `infer_collection_element_type` grows a `Deque__` arm (or the
# kind-gate stops admitting `Deque`), on BOTH backends.
from std.collections import Deque

struct S:
    int fd

int idx():
    print("IDX")
    return 0

void inc(int &n):
    n = n + 1

void main():
    Deque[S] d = Deque[S]()
    d.push(S(10))
    inc(&d[idx()].fd)
    print(d[0].fd)
